## 2. Connect to AWS Lightsail

**Run in Windows PowerShell:**

``` powershell
ssh -i "$env:USERPROFILE\Downloads\LightsailDefaultKey-ap-south-1.pem" ubuntu@13.232.198.72
```

## 3. Update Ubuntu and install packages

**Run in the Ubuntu SSH terminal:**

``` bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade -y
```

Install Nginx:

``` bash
sudo apt install nginx -y
```

Install PostgreSQL:

``` bash
sudo apt install postgresql postgresql-contrib -y
```

Check versions:

``` bash
node -v
npm -v
nginx -v
psql --version
```

## 4. Upload project without Git

The project was uploaded directly as an archive, without Git.

Archive name:

``` text
expense-tracker.tar.gz
```

Create the project directory and extract the archive:

``` bash
mkdir -p ~/app
tar -xzf ~/expense-tracker.tar.gz -C ~/app
```

Check the folders:

``` bash
ls -la ~/app
```

Expected project structure:

``` text
/home/ubuntu/app/
├── Backend/
└── frontend/
```

## 5. Backend deployment

Go to the backend directory:

``` bash
cd ~/app/Backend
```

Install dependencies:

``` bash
npm install
```

Create/edit the environment file:

``` bash
nano .env
```

Backend `.env` configuration (use your own private values):

``` env
PORT=5000
DB_DIALECT=postgres
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_PORT=5432
DB_NAME=expensetracker
DB_USER=appuser
DB_PASSWORD=YOUR_DB_PASSWORD
DB_LOGGING=false
DB_ALTER=false
JWT_SECRET=YOUR_SECRET
REDIS_ENABLED=false
```

Save and exit nano with `Ctrl+O`, Enter, then `Ctrl+X`.

Secure the environment file:

``` bash
chmod 600 .env
```

Start the backend for testing:

``` bash
npm start
```

Keep this terminal open while running it manually. Stop it with
`Ctrl+C`.

## 6. PostgreSQL database setup

Start PostgreSQL and enable it at boot:

``` bash
sudo systemctl start postgresql
sudo systemctl enable postgresql
```

Open the PostgreSQL shell:

``` bash
sudo -u postgres psql
```

Run these SQL commands inside `psql`:

``` sql
CREATE DATABASE expensetracker;
CREATE USER appuser WITH PASSWORD 'YOUR_DB_PASSWORD';
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON DATABASE expensetracker TO appuser;
```

Exit PostgreSQL:

``` sql
\q
```

Connect to the application database:

``` bash
sudo -u postgres psql -d expensetracker
```

List tables:

``` sql
\dt
```

The deployed database contains these five tables:

-   users
-   accounts
-   transactions
-   transfers
-   budgets

**Note:** If the database or user already exists, do not run the
corresponding `CREATE` command again. Do not share database passwords in
chat or commit them to source control.

## 7. Sequelize database synchronization

From the backend directory:

``` bash
cd ~/app/Backend
npm run db:sync
```

The sync script should call:

``` javascript
await sequelize.sync();
```

Check the tables:

``` bash
sudo -u postgres psql -d expensetracker -c '\dt'
```

## 8. Frontend deployment

Go to the frontend directory:

``` bash
cd ~/app/frontend
```

Install dependencies:

``` bash
npm install
```

Create/edit the frontend environment file:

``` bash
nano .env
```

Frontend API configuration:

``` env
VITE_API_URL=/api
```

Build the production frontend:

``` bash
npm run build
```

Vite generates production files in:

``` text
/home/ubuntu/app/frontend/dist
```

Create the Nginx web directory:

``` bash
sudo mkdir -p /var/www/expense-tracker
```

Copy the build files:

``` bash
sudo cp -a dist/. /var/www/expense-tracker/
```

Set ownership:

``` bash
sudo chown -R www-data:www-data /var/www/expense-tracker
```

## 9. Nginx configuration

Open the default Nginx site configuration:

``` bash
sudo nano /etc/nginx/sites-available/default
```

Configuration used:

``` nginx
server {
    listen 80 default_server;
    listen [::]:80 default_server;

    server_name _;

    root /var/www/expense-tracker;
    index index.html;

    location / {
        try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;
    }

    location /api/ {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:5000;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;

        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    }
}
```

Test the Nginx configuration:

``` bash
sudo nginx -t
```

Reload Nginx:

``` bash
sudo systemctl reload nginx
```

Enable Nginx at boot:

``` bash
sudo systemctl enable nginx
```

