## 11. AWS Lightsail firewall

In AWS Lightsail → Instance → Networking, configure:

  Port   Protocol   Purpose
  ------ ---------- ----------------------------------
  22     TCP        SSH
  80     TCP        HTTP website
  443    TCP        HTTPS, after HTTPS is configured

**Security:** Do not expose PostgreSQL port 5432 publicly. The backend
connects to PostgreSQL through localhost.

## 12. Commands for future updates

### Backend update

``` bash
cd ~/app/Backend
npm install
```

If the backend systemd service has been created and enabled, restart it:

``` bash
sudo systemctl restart expense-tracker-backend
```

View backend service logs:

``` bash
sudo journalctl -u expense-tracker-backend -f
```

**Important:** The systemd service setup was discussed but its creation
was not confirmed. Until it is configured, the backend may be running
manually with `npm start` and may stop when its terminal/session ends.
Check with:

``` bash
sudo systemctl status expense-tracker-backend
```

### Frontend update

``` bash
cd ~/app/frontend
npm install
npm run build
sudo cp -a dist/. /var/www/expense-tracker/
sudo chown -R www-data:www-data /var/www/expense-tracker
sudo systemctl reload nginx
```

